Ladybird matches a content script’s include and exclude globs against
the whole serialized URL, with “*” for any run of characters and “?” for
one, and matches an “about:”, “data:”, or “blob:” document as its
creator’s origin for a script with matchOriginAsFallback. Firefox does
both, with its MatchGlob for the globs, in MozDocumentMatcher::Matches()
and MatchesURI() (WebExtensionPolicy.cpp). Chromium has no include or
exclude globs for registered scripts, but matches by origin for
match_origin_as_fallback the same way. WebKit has neither.
